  "notes": "Replaces the NLCD executable stub and three permissive schema scaffolds with bounded native-grid candidate conformance. The source descriptor and class meanings remain unadmitted; no habitat inference or lifecycle/public authority. Six of 39 candidates are fixture-first on this stack; 33 remain unimplemented. Tightens five resolved scaffold findings, 863 to 858. Preserves historical receipts. Additional out-of-profile experiment: the full geometry suite in the raster pyproj 3.8.0 / PROJ 9.8.1 environment had 330 passing tests and one EPSG:6923 failure; reproduced in isolation without NLCD because us_noaa_kshpgn.tif was unavailable. The qualified general pyproj 3.7.2 pipeline lane passes. No locks, ballpark gates or network-grid settings were relaxed. GBIF PR 5963 merged into an intermediate branch; main-targeted delivery closure is being prepared separately. The policy-decision reference is accepted ADR-0029 repository placement/authority governance only, not source rights, model approval, data policy evaluation or release authorization. Final candidate is based on main-targeted closure PR 5964 at 664116397773bb3146f214a70bb26d3cd8e7203c; its own PR must also target main, never an intermediate branch."
